Tests for the patches in patches/libportal/, run by hand and in GitLab CI, see .gitlab-ci.yml.

libportal activation token: run-libportal-token.sh, libportal_token.py and openuri_portal.py
    Checks that libportal passes an activation token from a GTK 4 and a GTK 3 window when an application opens a URI
    through the OpenURI portal. Starts a headless mutter in a D-Bus session of its own, in which openuri_portal.py stands in for
    xdg-desktop-portal: it owns org.freedesktop.portal.Desktop, answers every OpenURI request as done and records it.
    libportal_token.py then runs a GTK 4 application and then a GTK 3 one, each of which shows a window and opens a URI
    through libportal for it, with xdp_parent_new_gtk(), as Ptyxis opens a link, and checks for each that the portal
    received one OpenURI request for that URI, with the window as its parent, and with an activation token in its
    options which mutter created for the application. Mutter does not see an event of the user behind the token, which the test does not need: it checks
    only that the token reaches the portal, which passes it on to the application it launches.

    libportal and its GTK helpers are tested without installing them, so the packages to test are extracted, and the
    test runs with the installed GTK 4 and GTK 3 and their introspection data:

      mkdir /tmp/mutter-root /tmp/libportal-root
      for p in mutter libmutter-18-0; do dpkg-deb -x /usr/local/lib/debs/${p}_*.deb /tmp/mutter-root; done
      for p in libportal1 libportal-gtk4-1 libportal-gtk3-1 gir1.2-xdp-1.0 gir1.2-xdpgtk4-1.0 gir1.2-xdpgtk3-1.0; do
        dpkg-deb -x /usr/local/lib/debs/${p}_*.deb /tmp/libportal-root
      done
      ./run-libportal-token.sh /tmp/mutter-root /tmp/libportal-root /tmp/libportal-token-test

    The script prints the request the portal received and one line for each check, and finally "RESULT: OK", and
    exits with 0. With Ubuntu's libportal, the requests carry no activation token, and the last two checks of each
    toolkit fail. The output directory has mutter's output as mutter.log, the clients' WAYLAND_DEBUG output as
    client-gtk4.log and client-gtk3.log, and the requests as requests.json.
